{
  ActionKind | doc "An action type: a task's `action_type` (`+0x10`, the `.dat`'s) and an action's type (`+0x8`),\none numbering. The `.dat` holds types the simulation does not run (the AI's, the scenario's),\nso the type is a newtype with named constants, not an enum: any value 0 or more the data\nholds is a type, and the named ones are values of the type. A field or a filter that holds −1\nfor none or any is `Option<ActionKind>`." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  AdjacentMode | doc "A building master's adjacent mode (`+0x980`, `adjacent_mode`): walls and gates join their\nneighbours (`FUN_1411ce890`). Every byte is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  Age | doc "An age option (`mStartingAge`, `+0x3c`, and `mEndingAge`, `+0x40`), and a tech tree unit's\nage: 0 the mode's default, 2 Feudal, 3 Castle, 4 Imperial, 5 post-Imperial, 6." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0),
  Amount | doc "An amount of a player attribute (a resource) as the game's `f32` holds it: what an object\nholds of its attribute (`+0x310`), what a unit carries at most (its master's\n`attribute_max_amount`, [`Amount::of_master`]), what a gather, a hunt or a drop-off moves.\nEach operator is the one `f32` operation the game does, in its order; a comparison is\n`f32`'s (a NaN compares false)." = Number,
  AmountRate | doc "An amount of a player attribute per second, as the game's `f32` holds it: what a dead\nobject's remains lose of their attribute a second (a master's `resource_decay`, `+0x620`),\nnegated on the hunted target whose decay a hunt stopped. Over [`Seconds`] it is an\n[`Amount`]. Each operator is the one `f32` operation the game does, in its order; a\ncomparison is `f32`'s (a NaN compares false)." = Number,
  ArcRatio | doc "A missile master's arc (the `.dat`'s `projectile_arc`, `+0x888`, the save's\n`ballistics_ratio`): 0 flies flat; else the launch makes the arc's rise of it and the way\n(`−arc × way × way` for one at most 0, `−arc × way` above)." = Number,
  AttackPriority | doc "A master's attack priority (`+0x92c`, `FUN_141202220`; the `.dat`'s combat part): a number\nthe unit AIs' attack checks read by value. Priority 3 limits most of them to the classes of\n`PRIORITY_3_CLASSES`; 1 and 2 let the lion and the predators choose anything; 0 holds the\nrams and the trebuchets to their own targets and 1 ranks the best target." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  AttributeId | doc "A player's attribute number (`player+0x100`'s array, the `.dat`'s attribute types, an effect's\nattribute argument): 0 or more. The first four are the resources (food, wood, stone, gold).\nThe simulation names the ones it tells apart (below); any other is a number the data holds\n([`AttributeId::numbered`]). A field that holds −1 for none is `Option<AttributeId>`." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  BlastDefense | doc "A master's blast defence (`area_effect_object_level`): the blast levels that reach it\n([`BlastLevel::reaches`])." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  BlastLevel | doc "The set's flag names joined by ` | `, unnamed bits as one hexadecimal number (`0x10`)." = String,
  BuildableOn | doc "A master's `can_be_built_on` (`+0x5e9`): 0 for most masters, 1 for others (the dead\nunits' among them), 2 for one master of build 158041's `.dat`. A foundation clears an\nobject of any but 0 off its footprint; a placement passes over one of 1 only." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  BuildingMaster | doc "What a building's completion (`FUN_1411dbb70` with 2) reads of its master, the `.dat`'s type\n80 values." = {
    adjacent_mode | AdjacentMode | doc "`+0x980`, `adjacent_mode`: walls and gates join their neighbours (`FUN_1411ce890`).",
