  CarryCapacity | doc "A master's carry capacity (`attribute_max_amount`, `+0x61c`): the whole amount an object of it\ncarries, a short the effects set, add to and scale (capped where the game caps them). Every\nshort is kept; `Amount::of_master` is the game's conversion." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
  Change | doc "How slot 0x148 changes an attribute (its second argument): set (0, slot 0x150), add (1, slot\n0x158) or multiply (2, slot 0x160); the masters' slots 0x18, 0x20, 0x28 and the objects' slots\n0x78, 0x80, 0x88 follow it." = [| 'Set, 'Add, 'Multiply |],
  ChangeMode | doc "How a technology's cost or research time changes (`'e'`'s and `'g'`'s third argument's low\nbyte, or kind 8's mode through its map): 0 sets, 2 scales by the amount less 1 (rounded half\naway from 1), any other adds. Every byte is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && 0 <= x && x <= 255),
  Charge | doc "A charge as the game's `f32` holds it: an object's charge (`+0x9e0`) and its master's most\n(`max_charge`, `+0x918`). A ready charge (its most for charge types 1 and 3, else 1) adds\nitself to the hit's attack. Each operator is the one `f32` operation the game does, in its\norder; a comparison is `f32`'s (a NaN compares false)." = Number,
  ChargeEvent | doc "A master's charge event (`mChargeEvent`, `+0x920`): the tiles a ready charge of type 6 or 7\n([`crate::objects::masters::ChargeKind::ranged`]) adds to the range (slot 0x2f8). Every short\nthe data or an effect leaves is kept." = std.contract.from_predicate (fun x => std.is_number x && x % 1 == 0 && -32768 <= x && x <= 32767),
